  <h1>About</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    I'm Fahmi Nugroho, a software engineer from Indonesia. I like building software that solves a
    real problem, and I like understanding why the solution works.
  </p>

  <p>
    I got into computers the way most people in this field did: a childhood fascination with
    machines that turned into a habit of typing in front of a laptop. I studied informatics because
    I wanted to know how the software underneath actually worked, and the curiosity stuck. These
    days I work mostly on web development, and I keep a running interest in machine learning and
    system design.
  </p>

  <p>
    Outside of writing application code, I spend time on the parts of engineering that do not show
    up in a screenshot: Linux and WSL, PostgreSQL and databases, networking, self-hosting, and
    deployment automation. I write technical documentation because a solution I cannot explain later
    is a solution I will have to rediscover.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    Build something useful. Learn something new. Share what you learn.
  </blockquote>

